# Cursor project rules

- Execute only the active phase or task packet. Stop at its exit gate.
- Read `docs/project-state.md` first. Load only files listed in the active guide's context budget.
- Before editing, state the intended outcome, touched areas, tests, assumptions, and non-goals.
- Do not invent requirements when a public contract is ambiguous. Ask one focused question or record an assumption in an ADR.
- Use strict Pydantic v2 boundary models with `extra="forbid"`; keep domain logic independent from FastAPI, Celery, SQLAlchemy, Streamlit, and model SDKs.
- Store time in integer milliseconds. Every derived metric declares unit, method version, confidence/status, and evidence references.
- Pass artifact IDs through queues, never frame arrays or model instances.
- Make stages idempotent and safe to retry. Write outputs atomically.
- Keep the API thin and heavy compute outside web workers.
- Treat uploads as hostile and subprocess calls as untrusted boundaries.
- Do not call shot boundaries narrative scenes. Do not present heuristic labels as artistic truth.
- Add only dependencies used in the active phase.
- Run the guide's verification commands and report actual results.
- Update `docs/project-state.md` in 120 lines or fewer, then stop.
